# Hospital Data Analysis Project

## Overview
This project is based on a dataset collected from King Fahd Hospital. The goal is to clean, process, and analyze the data, then build interactive dashboards to support better decision-making.

---

## Data Preparation
The process started by exploring the dataset and reviewing data types. Several issues were identified, including incorrect data formats, which were corrected.

A key step was handling the date and time fields. The original dataset contained combined date-time values, so they were separated into two columns:
- Date
- Time

This created multiple date-related fields, which required careful handling during the schema design phase.

---

## Data Modeling Approach
To handle the date-related challenge, two approaches were considered:

- Keeping date and time fields separated
- Using an alternating dimension approach in Power BI

Since the dataset is relatively small, the first approach was selected for simplicity and better performance.

After that:
- Keys were created
- Relationships between tables were defined
- The data model was built successfully

---

## Dashboard Development
After completing the data modeling phase, interactive dashboards were created using Power BI.

The dashboards include:

### Branch Performance Dashboard
- Tracks performance across hospital branches
- Compares key metrics between branches

### Patient Analysis Dashboard
- Analyzes patient trends
- Provides insights on key healthcare indicators    

---

## Insights and Recommendations
A final report was created to summarize findings and provide actionable recommendations aimed at improving hospital operations and decision-making.

---

## Tools & Technologies
- Power BI
- Data Cleaning & Transformation
- Data Modeling

---

## Conclusion
This project covers the full data analysis lifecycle, from raw data cleaning to building dashboards and delivering business insights.
